.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murk-agent-init 1  "init " 
.SH NAME
murk\-agent\-init \- Mint a scoped grant and print how to run the agent safely (experimental)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk agent init\fR [\fB\-\-allow\-tag\fR] [\fB\-\-ttl\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-name\fR> <\fB\-\-only\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mint a scoped grant and print how to run the agent safely (experimental)
.PP
With `\-\-allow\-tag`, murk first sets the agent allow\-list to those tags.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Grant name (used to revoke it later)
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fI<ONLY>\fR
Secrets the agent can read (repeatable, required)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-tag\fR \fI<ALLOW_TAG>\fR
Set the agent allow\-list to these tags before granting (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fI<TTL>\fR [default: 2h]
Time to live, e.g. 30m, 2h or 7d, up to 365d. Reads fail closed after expiry
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Where to write the agent key: a path, or `\-` for stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace a file already at \-\-out (refused by default)
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<VAULT>\fR [default: .murk]
Vault filename
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
